{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Behold, he goes out to the water.</b> To his latrine, for he made himself a deity, and because it is a place of filth it does not write 'come to Pharaoh.' For 'come' implies come with me." "<b>Behold, he goes out to the water.</b> To draw water for his foot. Another interpretation: in the manner of people who rise early in the morning to the bank of the river and wash from the waters of the river to brighten their eyes. Another interpretation: <b>behold, he goes out to the water</b> to stroll and hunt birds there by means of nets that he carries on his arm, like other kings, and there you will find him free to speak with him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:26.876345648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}